## Universal Conventions
- English for all code, comments, commit messages
- Greek only in UI-facing strings
- Never commit secrets, credentials, `.env` files
- All REST API responses follow `{ data, error, meta }` envelope
- WebSocket messages follow `{ type, payload }` envelope
- Dates/times always UTC in storage; format for display on frontend
- IDs are UUIDs v7 everywhere
- Feature branch naming: `feat/<scope>/<short-desc>`

## Code Quality Non-Negotiables
- No `any` type — ever
- No dead code or commented-out blocks in committed code
- All errors handled explicitly — no silent swallows
- Functions have a single responsibility
- No magic strings — use constants or enums

## Security Baseline
- Public routes: login, register, `/events` browse, `/events/:id` detail
- All other routes require authentication + correct role
- WebSocket connections authenticated via JWT query param on handshake
- Input validation on every form — never trust data before sending to API
- XSS prevention: never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with user data
- HTTPS / WSS enforced in production
